// sound.hby — sound files, notes and MIDI files.
//
//     use sound
//
//     sound.play "boom.wav"                   plays a sound file, once
//     sound.play_music "theme.mp3"            music, round and round
//     sound.play_note "A4", 500               a note, for half a second
//     sound.play_notes "C4 D4 E4 F4 G4", 300  a tune, a note at a time
//     sound.play_midi "song.mid"              a MIDI file
//     sound.wait                              until they've all finished
//
//     sound.part Tune                         a song, written as MIDI:
//     Tune.notes "E4 D4 C4:2", 1              parts of notes, in beats,
//     sound.song Song                         put together in a song
//     Song.add Tune
//     Song.save "tune.mid"
//
//     sound.recording Take = sound.record     records from the microphone,
//     Take.stop                               or an audio interface,
//     Take.save "take.wav"                    until stop
//     sound.set_monitoring true               (and heard as it's recorded)
//
//     sound.keyboard K = sound.open_keyboard  a MIDI keyboard: its notes
//     K.play_through "piano"                  heard at once, and told to
//     K.on_note played                        a handler (K.note, K.velocity)
//     sound.synthesizer S = sound.open_synthesizer   and a synthesizer,
//     S.play_note "C4", 500                   sent notes to play
//
// Everything plays at once, mixed together, and the program goes straight
// on: playing doesn't wait. A program that only plays sounds should end
// with sound.wait, or it ends before they're heard.
//
// Sound files can be WAV, MP3 or FLAC. Notes and MIDI files are played with
// a SoundFont's instruments: the one installed on the computer (FluidR3,
// "soundfont-fluid" on Arch, "fluid-soundfont-gm" on Debian), or any .sf2
// given to sound.set_soundfont. Without one, a simple synthesizer of
// Cabby's own plays them.
//
// The full reference is sound.md, next to this file.

// ---- the C side (runtime/sound.c); use the functions below instead

